    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0839" n="1797" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1797"/>

                <head>No. 28.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Garland to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 15, 1887</date>.
                        (Received.October 17.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to say, in reply to your
                    letter of the 13th instant, in relation to the release of the vessels <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Carolena, Onward</hi>, and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thornton</hi>, that before your request was received I had repeated the
                    instructions <pb facs="0840" n="1798" xml:id="pg1798"/> by telegraph to the
                    marshal for Alaska, and since its receipt have, as you suggested, supplemented
                    the telegram by a letter, both of these communications directing that the
                    instructions of January last be carried out.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. H. Garland.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
